📘 Extent Report Integration for Katalon 9.4.0
Confluence Ready Guide
🎯 Objective

This guide explains how to install the Extent Report Integration plugin for Katalon Studio 9.4.0.212 using the safest compatible version for the current project setup.

It is especially useful when the plugin appears as installed in Katalon Store, but does not load correctly inside Katalon Studio.

✅ Recommended Plugin Version
Extent Report Integration 8.0.2

This is the recommended version for the current environment because:

it is explicitly marked as compatible with Katalon version 9 and 10

the project is currently using Katalon Studio 9.4.0.212

it is more stable for this scenario than older 8.x releases

it is a safer option than newer major versions when compatibility is uncertain

🚫 Versions to Avoid for Now

To reduce risk during installation, do not start with these versions:

10.0.0

9.0.1

9.0.0

These may work in some environments, but for this project the safest first option is still 8.0.2.

📥 Step 1: Download the Correct Plugin Version

Open the Extent Report Integration page in Katalon Store and go to the Changelog or versions section.

Find the row for:

8.0.2

Then click the download icon for that version.

📂 Step 2: Place the Plugin in the Project Folder

After downloading the plugin .jar file, move it to the local project plugin directory:

C:\Users\BGS32GG\Workspace\gaia\Plugins
Important

Make sure:

the file is really inside the Plugins folder

the file is not still only inside Downloads

there is only one relevant version being tested first, to avoid confusion

🔄 Step 3: Restart Katalon Studio

After placing the plugin file in the correct folder:

close Katalon Studio

open Katalon Studio again

This restart is important so Katalon can re-read the local plugin directory.

⚙️ Step 4: Enable Local Plugin Loading

Inside Katalon Studio, open:

Project Settings > Plugins

Then select:

Local

or

Katalon Store and Local

Recommended option for this setup:

Katalon Store and Local

Then click:

Apply

Apply and Close

🔁 Step 5: Reload Plugins

After saving the plugin settings, go to:

Project > Reload Plugins

This forces Katalon to refresh the available plugin list.

✅ Step 6: Validate the Installation

After reloading, verify the plugin behavior.

Things to check:

the plugin errors in the editor are gone

imports related to Extent Report are resolved

the plugin is visible and usable by the project

no unresolved class errors remain for Extent libraries

Examples of classes that should now resolve correctly:

import com.aventstack.extentreports.ExtentReports
import com.aventstack.extentreports.ExtentTest
import com.aventstack.extentreports.MediaEntityBuilder
import com.aventstack.extentreports.reporter.ExtentSparkReporter
import com.aventstack.extentreports.reporter.configuration.Theme
🧪 Expected Result

When the installation is correct:

Katalon recognizes the Extent Report classes

the plugin can be used inside the project

the custom report builder can be updated to use the Extent integration

local project code compiles without unresolved import errors

🛠️ Troubleshooting
Plugin appears installed in Katalon Store, but not inside Katalon Studio

Check the following:

the .jar file is really inside the project Plugins folder

Katalon was fully restarted after copying the file

plugin loading is set to Local or Katalon Store and Local

Project > Reload Plugins was executed after reopening the project

Plugin list is empty

This can happen even when the plugin is downloaded. In that case:

confirm the plugin file exists in the correct folder

reopen Katalon again

keep only the required plugin version during testing

avoid mixing multiple Extent plugin versions at the same time

Import errors still appear

Common causes:

wrong plugin version

plugin file in the wrong folder

Katalon cache not refreshed yet

project reopened before the file copy finished

